cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper below."
title: >-
  Numerical checks for "Root-of-unity limit of the A_{n-1} lens elliptic
  gamma function solution of the star-star relation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yamazaki
    given-names: Masahito
    email: masahito.yamazaki@ipmu.jp
    affiliation: "Kavli IPMU (WPI), UTIAS, University of Tokyo"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/masahitoyamazaki/Lens_root-of-unity"
abstract: >-
  AI-generated Python scripts used for the numerical checks summarized in Appendix F
  (Table 2) of arXiv:2610.41438, covering the lens elliptic gamma function
  solution of the star-star relation, its root-of-unity limit and
  quasi-classical expansion, the resulting discrete spin solutions, elliptic
  sl(n) Kashiwara-Miwa type models (including the Quano-Fujii model), and the
  trigonometric limit.
keywords:
  - star-star relation
  - lens elliptic gamma function
  - root of unity
  - Yang-Baxter equation
  - integrable lattice models
  - Kashiwara-Miwa model
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
